      "role": "EN-READ-F",
      "source": "reading.text",
      "tts_text": "At the community music centre, repairing old instruments is part of the evening course. The tutor begins by checking the soundboard and listening for changes in resonance. Students practise cleaning each fretboard before touching a tuning peg. Learning to follow the woodgrain helps them avoid rough edges. One learner is interested in replacing a soundpost, while another prefers polishing the bridge. The luthier explains that careful listening often reveals a problem before any tool is used. By the end of the course, the group understands that patience matters as much as technical skill. Their first adjustment takes nearly an hour, but the clear tone is worth the effort.",
